Provenance

The mid-month transfer, messy-workbook and external-items ideas in 3 payroll
tax validation cards adapt scenarios S03, S08 and S07 from
Tim-Claessen/payrolltaxdatasets, commit
8f7d9bb79578fc2b62c3885c54640695cb4355b7 (CC0-1.0), inspected on 5 November
2026: https://github.com/Tim-Claessen/payrolltaxdatasets. The cards use newly
fabricated amounts and no upstream rows, identifiers, rates or generator code.
The remaining jurisdiction cards are original. Existing grouping and
threshold-edge cards already cover the S04 and S10 topics, and the back-pay
card covers the back-pay topic of S06. Two
Queensland cards added on 13 November 2026 adapt the cancelled-run and
off-cycle-run ideas of S06 and the fringe-benefit, share-scheme and
redundancy ideas of S07 from the same commit, with newly fabricated amounts.

Workflow skills for Australian public-practice and contracting-business
accounting, written independently, from scratch, in my own time and on my own
equipment.


The v0.3.0 development expansion uses OpenAccountants Australian topic names
for gap identification. No OpenAccountants Guide bodies were copied or
adapted. The new workflow text is original; primary-source starting points
and their retrieval limitations are recorded beside each skill.

